From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Wright <wright@esrf.fr>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 21:37:57 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] decompress: copy overlapping matches with offset 8..15
 without a store-to-load chain

A match whose offset is 8..15 bytes overlaps its own output.  Both decode
loops copied it 8 bytes at a time (LZ4_wildCopy8), each load reading bytes
that the previous store had just written, so the copy runs at the speed of
store-to-load forwarding (~2.6 GB/s for a long match on Zen 4).

Bitshuffled 16-bit detector frames hit this constantly: a block whose top
bit-planes are all zero ends in a ~5 kB zero run that lz4 encodes as one
match with offset 8..15.

LZ4_copy_overlap_doubling() writes such a match exactly up to its end:
- if the 8..15-byte pattern is all zero (its first and last 8 bytes cover
  it), with memset;
- otherwise by copying [src, op) onto op, which doubles the periodic region,
  so non-overlapping copies of growing length reproduce the match.
The output is byte-identical; nothing is written past the end of the match.

Used for 8 <= offset < 16 in the fast loop (LZ4_memcpy_using_offset_base)
and, for matches longer than 16 bytes, in the safe loop.

Measured (LZ4_decompress_safe on 8 kB bitshuffle-LZ4 blocks, EPYC 9454):
long zero runs at offset 8..15: 2.6 -> ~33 GB/s; Eiger2 16M dense frame
4.1 -> 26.5 GB/s; other data unchanged (-3 % on a Poisson-1000 frame).

Validated: tests/ `make test`; fuzzer/frametest/decompress-partial with
LZ4_FAST_DEC_LOOP=0; `make usan`; fuzzer/frametest under clang ASan;
ossfuzz decompress, round_trip, round_trip_stream, round_trip_hc,
decompress_frame and round_trip_frame under clang ASan+UBSan (5 min each);
a targeted round-trip/corruption stress test (~11M matches with offset
8..15, ASan+UBSan, fast loop on and off).

Local patch for bslz4_to_sparse (on top of v1.10.0); not submitted upstream.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 lib/lz4.c | 35 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 32 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/lib/lz4.c b/lib/lz4.c
index a2f7abee..dcb49271 100644
--- a/lib/lz4.c
+++ b/lib/lz4.c
@@ -490,6 +490,30 @@ static const int      dec64table[8] = {0, 0, 0, -1, -4,  1, 2, 3};
 #  endif
 #endif
 
+/* Used by both decode loops (with or without LZ4_FAST_DEC_LOOP). */
+LZ4_FORCE_INLINE void
+LZ4_copy_overlap_doubling(BYTE* op, const BYTE* src, BYTE* const end)
+{
+    /* An overlapping match: [src, op) is a pattern of 8..15 bytes that repeats
+     * up to end.  If it is all zero (its first and last 8 bytes cover it),
+     * write the zeros with memset.  Otherwise copy [src, op) onto op: that
+     * doubles the periodic region, so non-overlapping copies of growing length
+     * reproduce the match exactly, with no store-to-load dependency chain. */
+    U64 head, tail;
+    LZ4_memcpy(&head, src, 8);
+    LZ4_memcpy(&tail, op - 8, 8);
+    if ((head | tail) == 0) {
+        MEM_INIT(op, 0, (size_t)(end - op));
+        return;
+    }
+    while (op < end) {
+        size_t n = (size_t)(op - src);
+        if (n > (size_t)(end - op)) n = (size_t)(end - op);
+        LZ4_memcpy(op, src, n);
+        op += n;
+    }
+}
+
 #if LZ4_FAST_DEC_LOOP
 
 LZ4_FORCE_INLINE void
@@ -507,9 +531,8 @@ LZ4_memcpy_using_offset_base(BYTE* dstPtr, const BYTE* srcPtr, BYTE* dstEnd, con
         srcPtr -= dec64table[offset];
         dstPtr += 8;
     } else {
-        LZ4_memcpy(dstPtr, srcPtr, 8);
-        dstPtr += 8;
-        srcPtr += 8;
+        LZ4_copy_overlap_doubling(dstPtr, srcPtr, dstEnd);   /* 8 <= offset < 16 */
+        return;
     }
 
     LZ4_wildCopy8(dstPtr, srcPtr, dstEnd);
@@ -2403,6 +2426,12 @@ LZ4_decompress_generic(
                 continue;
             }
 
+            if (offset >= 8 && offset < 16 && length > 16) {
+                if (cpy > oend-LASTLITERALS) { goto _output_error; }
+                LZ4_copy_overlap_doubling(op, match, cpy);
+                op = cpy;
+                continue;
+            }
             if (unlikely(offset<8)) {
                 LZ4_write32(op, 0);   /* silence msan warning when offset==0 */
                 op[0] = match[0];
-- 
2.49.0

